  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "環境倫理學",
    "sub_ename": "ENVIRONMENTAL ETHICS",
    "describe_ch": "本課程是以環境倫理的理論為核心，除了引介理論的內容與相關的議題，並關注於學習者能否分辨對於環境議題，自身判斷的價值觀、倫理規範或理論依據為何，以使學習者確認自身的價值觀是單一還是多元，並盡可能地走向多元價值觀。此外，本課程以專題式學習的方式，透過主題與相關案例的分析，以及行動策略的發想與宣達，期使學習者能在小組討論、場域觀察、分享反思等作為中，練習並觀察自身在活動中的思考變化，進而能培養對於問題的敏感度，以及持續的反思自己的環境倫理觀。",
    "describe_eh": "This course is centered on the theory of environmental ethics. In addition to introducing theoretical content and related issues, it focuses on whether learners can identify their own values, ethical standards, or theoretical basis for judgment regarding environmental issues. The aim is to help learners realize whether their values are singular or plural and to encourage a shift towards a more diverse set of values. Furthermore, this course adopts a project-based learning approach, through theme and case analysis, as well as the development and promotion of action strategies. The goal is to enable learners to practice and observe changes in their thoughts during activities such as group discussions, field observations, and reflective sharing. This process aims to foster sensitivity to environmental issues and the continuous reflection on environmental ethical views of their own.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "引導學習者思考環境議題的出現是科學、人文與社會各種觀點衝突的結果，藉以突顯倫理思考之重要性。",
      "describe_en": "To guide learners to think that the emergence of environmental issues is the result of conflicts between scientific, humanistic, and social perspectives, thereby highlighting the importance of ethical thinking."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "引導學習者建立釐清自身道德判斷的基礎概念，了解在判斷過程中的思考，被歸類於哪種理論，合理性與有效性的範圍，以及可能的缺失何在。",
      "describe_en": "To guide learners to establish the foundational concepts for clarifying their own moral judgments, understanding which theory their thinking falls under in the judgment process, the scope of its rationality and validity, and potential shortcomings."
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "describe_ch": "引導學習者能由因應環境議題發展而出現的理論，建立釐清自身道德判斷的進階概念，接受多元的價值觀。",
      "describe_en": "To guide learners to develop advanced concepts for clarifying their moral judgments based on the theories that arise in response to environmental issues, and to embrace diverse values."
    }
  ],
